  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "ScGiESbIP6hornPRA1xN9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 245,
      "y": 162,
      "width": 1821,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 467704882,
      "version": 2319,
      "versionNonce": 974832946,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794413185409,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a reel or shorts feed generation system\n\n1. Functional requirements : \n    1. Feed Generation : User recieves personalized, infinite scroll of short videos.\n    2. System must record the ionteraction of every reel - like , share , follow and views.\n    3. System must surface new content and learn from new user prefrences without relying on historical data\n    4. Uploading of reels should be instant and made available for the recommendation.\n    5. System should recommend friends liked or currently trending reels too or can hit a reset button to reset the suggestions.\n\n2. Non - Functional requirement : \n    1. Ultra low latency for feed generation < 200 ms\n    2. Massive scale : Can expect upto 2B DAU and Millions of uploads.\n    3. High throughput in case of interactions\n    4. Consistency in online features like a video getting viral in last 5 mins\n    5. Availability in case of feed.\n\n3. Back of the envelope :\n    1. 2 B DAU with Read QPS = 2B * Opeining app atelast 5 times * scrolling upto 40 vids = 40 B / 100,000 = 40,000 QPS\n    2. Write QPS 40B views * 4 events per view / 100,000 s = 1.6 Million QPS\n    3. Storage = Assuming 100 M active videos of 2 B users with 10% of uploads = 2B * 10% * 5MB (video size) = 200 M * 5 MB = 1 PB of storage and 100M * 5 = 500 TB of cache\n\n4. API Designing : \n    1. Feed : GET /v1/feed/reels\n        {user_id : id, video_id, author_id , media_url, description, duration_sec}\n    2. Interactions : POST /v1/analytics/event \n        {user_id , timestamp , video_id, event_type, value_ms}\n5. Data Models and Entities \n    1. Video Metadata : video_id (PK), author_id (Index), media_url, description, duration_sec = cassandra for metadata and s3 for actual mp4 files\n    2. interactions : user_id (Partition Key), timestamp (Clustering Key), video_id, event_type, value_ms = cassandra\n    3. user : user_id, username, region, account_created = postgreSQL\n\n6. High level design : ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a reel or shorts feed generation system\n\n1. Functional requirements : \n    1. Feed Generation : User recieves personalized, infinite scroll of short videos.\n    2. System must record the ionteraction of every reel - like , share , follow and views.\n    3. System must surface new content and learn from new user prefrences without relying on historical data\n    4. Uploading of reels should be instant and made available for the recommendation.\n    5. System should recommend friends liked or currently trending reels too or can hit a reset button to reset the suggestions.\n\n2. Non - Functional requirement : \n    1. Ultra low latency for feed generation < 200 ms\n    2. Massive scale : Can expect upto 2B DAU and Millions of uploads.\n    3. High throughput in case of interactions\n    4. Consistency in online features like a video getting viral in last 5 mins\n    5. Availability in case of feed.\n\n3. Back of the envelope :\n    1. 2 B DAU with Read QPS = 2B * Opeining app atelast 5 times * scrolling upto 40 vids = 40 B / 100,000 = 40,000 QPS\n    2. Write QPS 40B views * 4 events per view / 100,000 s = 1.6 Million QPS\n    3. Storage = Assuming 100 M active videos of 2 B users with 10% of uploads = 2B * 10% * 5MB (video size) = 200 M * 5 MB = 1 PB of storage and 100M * 5 = 500 TB of cache\n\n4. API Designing : \n    1. Feed : GET /v1/feed/reels\n        {user_id : id, video_id, author_id , media_url, description, duration_sec}\n    2. Interactions : POST /v1/analytics/event \n        {user_id , timestamp , video_id, event_type, value_ms}\n5. Data Models and Entities \n    1. Video Metadata : video_id (PK), author_id (Index), media_url, description, duration_sec = cassandra for metadata and s3 for actual mp4 files\n    2. interactions : user_id (Partition Key), timestamp (Clustering Key), video_id, event_type, value_ms = cassandra\n    3. user : user_id, username, region, account_created = postgreSQL\n\n6. High level design : ",
